  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Being able to launch multiple clients into a single test build instance has historically been very tedious and difficult.\nAn extremely useful feature for the QuickLauncher to aid in this effort would be to provide a way to pick a local test build as the world to launch the clients into.\nCurrently the only reasonable way to do this is to have a menu script option for copying the most recent local build url and then pasting it into the Join tab's instance link input.\n(I use the following to accomplish that)\n```\n[MenuItem(\"VRChat SDK/Utilities/Copy Local Test Instance\")]\npublic static void GetLocalTestInstance()\n{\n    GUIUtility.systemCopyBuffer = VRC.SDKBase.Editor.VRC_SdkBuilder.GetLastUrl();\n    Debug.Log($\"Instance URL Copied: {VRC.SDKBase.Editor.VRC_SdkBuilder.GetLastUrl()}\");\n}\n```\nThe way I see this being the most useful, would be for the VQL to scrub the appdata folder for any VRCW files (standalone windows only obviously) and present them in a dropdown, preferably sorted DESC by modified timestamp, so the creator can choose which build to load up (the top one being the most recently built).\nAlso, I think to provide additional context to the creator, next to each of the entries of the dropdown, show the relative amount of time (minutes/hours/days) it's been since the build was made (the modified timestamp delta). This would be a fun data point for the creator of relatively how long it's been since they worked on said world.",
